# PHP coding standards

This Cursor rule mirrors the `php-coding` skill index. Load the `php-coding` skill, then read the reference each change maps to from its `references/` directory.

- **Deterministic beats prose.** If php-cs-fixer, PHPStan, PHPUnit, or `composer audit` fails the build when a rule is broken, run the tool. Do not restate the rule.
- **The pin is PHP 8.4.** PHP 8.5 additions are hints until the repository requires them.

| The change touches | Run | Read |
|---|---|---|
| formatting, naming, PER layout | `vendor/bin/php-cs-fixer fix --dry-run --diff` | `style.md` |
| types, comparisons, exceptions, enums, `readonly`, 8.4 and 8.5 features | `vendor/bin/phpstan analyse` | `idioms.md` |
| tests | `vendor/bin/phpunit` | `testing.md` |
| a public API other packages use | `vendor/bin/roave-backward-compatibility-check` | `compatibility.md` |
| SQL, output escaping, passwords, tokens, `unserialize`, shell, input paths or URLs | `composer audit` | `security.md` |
| a PSR interface such as `ServerRequestInterface`, `MiddlewareInterface`, `LoggerInterface`, `ContainerInterface`, `ClientInterface`, `ClockInterface` | `vendor/bin/phpstan analyse` | `psr.md` |
| Guzzle, Monolog, OpenTelemetry, Slim, Symfony components | none | `guzzle.md`, `monolog.md`, `opentelemetry.md`, `slim.md`, `symfony-components.md` |
| lint config | none | the `php-lint-setup` skill |

If a workflow already owns the review seat, that reviewer reads the references. Do not dispatch `php-reviewer` beside it.
